  "id": "adaptation-period",
  "term": "adaptation period",
  "definition": "An adaptation period is the initial phase after a person is exposed to a continuous, predictable disturbance, before their behavior settles into a more stable pattern. In this source, it refers to the early stage of balancing during repeated platform movements, when responses change over time before reaching steadier performance.",
